6. Relationship to SSM-JTK

SSM-JA is structurally connected to SSM-JTK and applies the deterministic
transit-kernel direction developed within that project to the SSM-JA
browser-native observational reference implementation.

SSM-JTK follows its own separate licensing terms.

Nothing in this license changes, overrides, or relicenses SSM-JTK materials
outside the SSM-JA licensing boundary.

Use of SSM-JA does not grant governance authority over SSM-JTK, the Shunyaya
Framework, or any other Shunyaya project.

7. Verification and Assurance Claims

A passing integrity check, deterministic replay result, verification result,
checksum result, or other reported result applies only to the declared files,
inputs, embedded structures, release version, supported scope, and verification
boundary associated with that result.

Modified files, changed kernels, changed rules, changed inputs, changed embedded
structures, or changed verification artifacts require their own verification.

Redistribution, modification, or use of the covered materials must not imply
third-party verification, institutional certification, standards recognition,
production qualification, astronomical certification, professional Jyotish
approval, legal approval, regulatory approval, or endorsement by the original
project maintainers unless such a claim has been separately and expressly
authorized.

Deterministic reproducibility does not by itself establish universal astronomical
truth, universal observational accuracy, or professional advisory correctness.

